Both files syntax-clean. All 16 collector fixes and 12 scanner security controls verified present. Here's the complete accounting:

16 collector fixes — what each one actually does
Fix	Issue	Resolution
FIX-01	SoapySDRKwargs.get() crash	dict(results[0]).get() — cast before dict API call
FIX-02	TOCTOU on temp IQ dir	os.open(dir, O_DIRECTORY) then os.fstat(dir_fd) — attacker cannot swap the dir between those two calls
FIX-03	Double-close after os.fdopen()	Removed bare os.close(fd) in except — fdopen owns the fd; any second close is undefined behavior
FIX-04	Tower CSV written then chmod() — race window	_open_output_file() with `O_EXCL
FIX-05	Meta append used plain open() — no permission control	_open_append_file() with `O_WRONLY
FIX-06	O_NOFOLLOW missing from all file creates	Added to every _open_output_file() call — blocks symlink redirect attacks
FIX-07	makedirs() then chmod() — race between creation and permission set	_safe_umask(0o077) context wraps makedirs() — dir created at 0o700 atomically
FIX-08	self.decoded = [] on GSMBurstDecoder accumulated frames across calls	Removed entirely — each decode_bcch() call is stateless
FIX-09	compute_psd: samples[:nfft] silently produced wrong-bin FFT when len(samples) < nfft	Guard: requires >= nfft//4 samples; zero-pads to nfft; returns empty arrays if insufficient
FIX-10	_validate_int_field: int("65535.0") raises ValueError; srsran emits float strings	int(float(str(value))) — handles both "65535" and "65535.0"
FIX-11	FCCTowerDatabase.check(): None mnc → "None" string → never matches stored key → false CRITICAL	str(mnc) if mnc is not None else "" — matches stored "" keys
FIX-12	_sanitize_csv_field: while loop on all-injection-char input could spin forever	lstrip("=+-@\t\r\n") — single O(n) pass, no loop
FIX-13	read_samples: sr.ret == 0 with no error → infinite loop on hardware stall	Stall counter; breaks after MAX_READ_STALLS (10) consecutive zero returns
FIX-14	session created inside try — finally block hit NameError if __init__ threw	session = CollectionSession() before try; _closed flag makes close() idempotent
FIX-15	_running bare global bool — no memory barrier between signal handler and main thread	threading.Event() — _running.clear() / _running.is_set() with proper synchronization
FIX-16	No integrity seal on evidence files	SHA-256 of all 4 output files + chain hash binding them to session timestamp, written as _manifest.sha256

Scanner security controls (Part 2)

The scanner has no hardware or subprocess surface — its attack surface is entirely the RF-collected JSON it reads. All 12 controls address that:

    Input file size capped at 100 MB before read; content length re-checked after read
    JSON array length capped at 50,000 records
    Every field in every record validated through typed sanitizers before touching output
    Severity and anomaly type values whitelisted — unknown values become "UNKNOWN" not silently passed through
    Statute strings matched against ^(47|18|28|42) U.S.C. §... regex — arbitrary strings from RF data cannot appear in the report as legal citations
    Float fields (power_dbm, freq_mhz) validated finite and in physically plausible range — NaN/Inf from corrupt input cannot propagate
    All output files O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW|0o600
    SHA-256 manifest covers input file + both output files; re-hashes input at report time and flags if it changed between load and write

